<style>
  .sankey-shell {
    max-width: 1200px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 16px;
  }

  #film-sankey-container {
    position: relative;
    background: #f8f8f8;
    border: 1px solid #e0e0e0;
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 12px;
  }

  #film-sankey-tooltip {
    position: absolute;
    pointer-events: none;
    padding: 8px 10px;
    border-radius: 6px;
    background: rgba(32, 32, 32, 0.92);
    color: #fff;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    opacity: 0;
    transition: opacity 120ms ease;
    z-index: 10;
  }

  #film-sankey-tooltip.visible {
    opacity: 1;
  }

  #film-sankey-notes {
    margin-top: 12px;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    color: #333;
  }

  #film-sankey-notes .note-item {
    margin-bottom: 6px;
  }
</style>

<div class="sankey-shell">
  <h1>Studio and Streaming M&A (Sankey)</h1>
  <p>
    Major media mergers visualized as flows. Link thickness shows deal value (USD billions).
    Netflix → Warner Bros. Discovery is marked as announced; historical deals include AOL–Time Warner, AT&T–Time Warner,
    Disney–21st Century Fox, and Sony–Columbia. The Telecommunications Act of 1996 loosened U.S. media ownership caps,
    accelerating telecom–media combos.
  </p>

  <div id="film-sankey-container">
    <div id="film-sankey"></div>
    <div id="film-sankey-tooltip"></div>
  </div>

  <div id="film-sankey-notes"></div>
</div>

